  "open_decisions": [
    "Registry v4 (user 2026-10-25): SERVO-DOOR-01 and SERVO-WINDOW-01 are open/close motors without angle control on GPIO19 and GPIO21. position_degrees 90 = open and 0 = closed are codes, not angles; CTRL-ESP32-ACT-01 turns them into the pulses of the user's tested sketch (around 90: door open -90 / close 0, window open -90 / close +90, 1000-2000 us) and drives nothing before the first command. SERVO-DOOR-02 (bathroom door) was removed from the model: ID kept, not_wired.",
    "Registry v4 ESP8266 (user 2026-10-25): CTRL-ESP8266-LED-01 drives LED-LIVING-01 (D0), LED-AIRCON-01 (D1) and FAN-01 (D2, moved from the ESP32), HIGH = on, all LOW at power-on (user's tested sketch). The model has nothing else: every other device keeps its official ID as not_wired with assignment_status removed_from_model (UI and app do not list them).",
    "FAN-01 accepts set_switch only until PWM (set_level) is verified on hardware.",
    "LED single-colour state encoding: steady red = power on, slow blink = quiet/mute/deferred (set_color pattern)."
  ]
